taking a hit from uk sensors a court  battle with the howdy duty show and a  very real negative impact on our  ecosystem you won't believe the truth  behind the teenage mutant ninja turtles  the turtles made their first appearance  in may 1984 in the pages of their  self-titled comic co-creators kevin  eastman and peter laird self-published  their reptilian romp under the banner of  mirage studios a name they reportedly  chose because they had no actual  publishing company when the turtles  popularity began to boom alongside the  release of their first cartoon in 1987  archie comics launched their own comic  book series teenage mutant ninja turtles  adventures to capitalize on the show's  success the turtle's original mirage  series ran for two volumes a third  volume which was brutal violent and  largely considered by fans to be  non-canon was published under image  comics in 1996 the series returned to  the mirage fold for volume 4 which ran  from 2001 to 2014 a tie-in comic to the  2003 tv series was published by  dreamwave which only lasted for seven  issues idw publishing has also been  putting out a tmnt comic since 2011  which has had more than 250 issues to  date aside from their ongoing series the  turtles have also made crossover  appearances and comics published by  darkhorse boom studios in dc however the  turtles have yet to officially appear in  the marvel universe which is ironic  considering how their very first story  was written in a way that tied into the  origin of the hero of hell's kitchen  himself daredevil  any tmnt fan is familiar with their  origin story four turtles in the new  york sewers end up in the care of  splinter a martial arts expert who is  also a rat when a canister of  radioactive ooze falls into the sewers  transforming the turtles and their  master the newly mutated ninja warrior  names his four adopted sons after  renaissance artists and teaches them how  to fight however there have been at  least two significant occasions where  the crime fighting quartet welcomed the  fifth mutant turtle to their team and in  both instances that new member was a  girl the 1997 tv show ninja turtles the  next mutation introduced a major change  to the tmt mythos in the form of venus  de milo the fifth turtle venus  apparently mutated alongside the other  four but was adopted and raised by a  chinese shinobi master she wore a  braided light blue mask and was a  skilled magic practitioner she didn't  quite catch on in fact legend has it  that peter laird hated her with such a  passion that he banned her from  appearing in any future turtle  adaptations about two decades later a  fifth turtle would join the group once  again but this time a little differently  first appearing in 2015's teenage mutant  ninja turtles number 51 the idw series  introduced janika a former assassin who  was mutated into a turtle when leonardo  and donatello gave her an emergency  blood transfusion to save her life she  wears a yellow bandana and uses a pair  of claws evocative of the marvel hero  wolverine  the turtle successfully took the pop  culture world by storm in the 90s but  that doesn't mean the franchise didn't  have to make some compromises along the  way one of the most infamous examples in  the retitling of the series and the  replacement of one of the lead signature  weapons in order to make it past censors  in the united kingdom throughout the 80s  and 90s the british government was  particularly iffy about portrayals of  violence in various forms of media for  some reason the idea of the ninja a  stealthy assassin from halfway across  the globe just didn't sit right with uk  sensors that was why in the uk and other  european countries they were known as  the teenage mutant hero turtles the  show's name wasn't the only adjustment  that tmnt or tmht had to make for  british audiences though uk sensors also  weren't too keen on michelangelo's  nunchucks weapons strongly associated  with ninjas therefore michelangelo's  main weapon in the cartoon was changed  to become a grappling hook this  censorship rule also necessitated a  rather odd edit in the 1991 movie  teenage mutant ninja turtles 2 the  secret of the ooze centers mandated that  a scene showing michelangelo's swinging  sausage links as makeshift weapons be  cut from the final film an amusing note  from the sensors read reduced to minimum  dazzling display of swinging sausages  indistinguishable from chain  next time i'll sticks mustard  when the ninja turtles first jumped onto  the scene it seemed like the franchise  could do no wrong the cartoon was a  massive hit the movies made fans happy  and toy sales were off the charts that's  likely what brought about the idea of a  live concert tour sponsored and promoted  by pizza hut in 1990 the coming out of  our shells tour featured the four  turtles trading in their ninja weapons  for musical instruments leonardo was on  the bass guitar rafael was on the drums  donatello was the keyboarders and  michelangelo was the guitarist and lead  singer an actual band dressed up in  infamously bad tmnt costumes with denim  vest went on a year-long tour across the  united states performing original songs  on stage their first performance was a  live pay-per-view broadcast from radio  city music hall in new york the central  story of the musical tour revolved  around the turtle's nemesis the shredder  and his plan to steal the world's music  needless to say the coming out of our  shells tour certainly wasn't a highlight  of the tmnt fandom even though it was  successful enough to merit a smaller  follow-up tour in 1992  most people know chuck lorre for his  work on popular sitcoms such as roseanne  two and a half men and the big bang  theory however one of the lesser known  accomplishments of the king of sitcoms  was a major contribution to tmnt's  popularity he wrote the iconic theme  song from the 1987 cartoon in an  interview with indy wire lori shared how  three decades ago he and his co-writer  dennis brown were faced with an  incredibly short turnaround time for the  song saying we wrote it in an afternoon  and we recorded it in an evening at the  time  lori was trying to kick-start his career  by writing songs and scripts for tv  shows and was particularly interested in  the turtles gig someone else got the job  at first but when they didn't complete  the task on time the production team had  no choice but to contact laurie and give  him the assignment on a tight 48-hour  timeline lori and brown read the mirage  comics for inspiration then made the  most out of their meager two thousand  dollar budget by booking a studio in los  angeles from midnight until 8 8am  laurie also revealed that originally the  teenage mutant ninja turtles cartoon was  only going to last for 6 episodes he  said of the show's lasting legacy the  fact that the song still means anything  to anyone anywhere is just wonderful  it's become this phenomenon i'm very  proud to be attached to  the worldwide popularity of the tmnt  franchise has allowed for some truly  diverse interpretations of the  characters perhaps one of the best  examples was the japanese animated  special teenage mutant ninja turtles  legend of the super mutants also known  as mutant turtles superman legend this  two-part direct-to-video original video  animation was released in 1996 and was  created as a companion cartoon to the  metal mutant and super mutant action  figures the limited series also brought  back some of the voice actors from the  japanese dub of the 1987 cartoon legend  of the super mutants sees the four  turtles gaining the ability to transform  into armored super turtles through the  use of mystical gems called muted stones  their evil counterparts the shredder  krang bebop and rocksteady could also  transform using the muted stones with  shredder in particular having a striking  dragon-like alternate form further  strengthening the comparisons between  legend of the super mutants it also  borrows from tokusatsu's troops by  allowing the super turtles to merge into  a stronger entity called the turtle  saint the second part was even more  bizarre depicting the four turtles as  having the power to shift into elemental  animal forms through the use of mystical  suits of armor called metal beasts  the cover of marvel's captain america  comics number one features the sentinel  of liberty punching adolf hitler in the  face a powerful image that immediately  tells the reader who steve rogers is and  what he stands for interestingly enough  a teenage mutant ninja turtle had a  similar encounter in the comics one that  in the turtle's reality actually helped  put an end to the second world war in  issue number 64 of archie comics teenage  mutant ninja turtles adventures the  future versions of leonardo donatello  and raphael use a time slip generator to  go back to the past and stop a human  brain in a robot suit from wreaking  havoc they land in nazi germany where  they learn that the brain powering their  robot adversary belonged to the mad  tyrant himself a scuffle quickly ensues  during which the one-eyed future raf  gets the opportunity to deck the  dictator in the dome upon retrieving the  brain the turtles quickly open up a  portal to their own time but not before  convincing hitler that they're actually  brain-snatching demons in a vain attempt  to foil their plans hitler responds by  promptly pulling out a luger and blowing  his brains out  ask any longtime fan of tmnt to tell you  a single word that they connect with the  series and there's a good chance they'll  respond with one particular iconic  catchphrase  a nonsensical term coined by buffalo bob  smith for the howdy duty show in 1949  surfers began to popularize the phrase  in the 1960s there's no doubt however  that the turtles use of cowabunga helped  cement the term's popularity in the eyes  and mouths of the general public  according to david wise head writer of  the 1987 tmnt series he wrote cowabunga  into michelangelo's dialogue to give him  some added character but when the  party-loving reptile uttered the phrase  in the pilot episode it just clicked and  cowabunga became the turtle's battle cry  however this prompted buffalo bob to sue  eastman and laird for their use of the  term he invented they eventually settled  out of court for 50 thousand dollars but  due to its enduring popularity in the  tmnt mythos the phrase continues to pop  up in different on-screen incarnations  of the team  the most popular species of pet turtle  in the world is arguably the red-eared  slider their cheap price and  availability made them easily obtainable  in the u.s until 1975 when concerns  about salmonella negatively impacted the  turtle trade however less than two  decades later the demand for pet turtles  soared anew because of the tmnt  phenomenon and worsened a major invasive  species problem that continues to plague  the world's ecosystem to this very day  based on reports cited by the u.s  geological survey there is indeed a  direct connection between the tmnt  television cartoon craze as they called  it and the sudden boom in red-eared  slider populations worldwide u.s turtle  exports from 1989 to 1997 experienced a  staggering 257 percent increase as  thousands of children across the world  begged their parents for their very own  turtle pets at home there was a problem  though when young pet owners often  decided that they no longer wanted the  responsibility of caring for their  turtles they would release them into  nearby lakes or rivers unfortunately  red-eared sliders are infamous not just  for their tendency to carry disease but  also for being bigger and more  competitive than many native turtle  species when an invasive species is  introduced into a new environment it  usually spells doom for other species in  the ecosystem in fact invasive species  are the second greatest driver of  biodiversity loss worldwide  the seeds of the tmnt franchise were  planted in 1983 thanks to a random  illustration that kevin eastman sketched  while he was staying at peter laird's  place at the time they were working on a  different comic but the ridiculousness  of eastman's doodle a turtle wearing a  bandana and standing on two legs with a  pair of nunchucks strapped to his arms  made them reconsider their priorities  while the other turtles would come to  fruition soon after it was michelangelo  that started it all michelangelo is  often portrayed across various media  adaptations as the least serious among  the turtles the comic relief that  balances out leonardo's stoicism  rafael's ill-temper and donatello's  awkward nerdiness in most iterations  he's also the least skilled fighter  despite his tremendous unrealized  potential perhaps that's why eastman and  laird thought it would be appropriate  for him to be the lone surviving turtle  in a dystopian future story that they've  been planning since 1987. the 2020 comic  series tmnt the last ronin features a  much older michelangelo on a mission to  avenge his brothers after they were  killed by descendants of the shredder  armed with his brother's weapons this  michelangelo was violent fearless and  determined to take out the foot clan  once and for all there's something very  unsettling about seeing the class clown  in a different more brutal light aside  from serving as a love letter to the  various versions of the tmnt the 2009  animated film turtles forever made one  thing clear in every universe that has  the turtles there's an iteration of the  villainous shredder to serve as their  foil however this wasn't always meant to  be the case if the first ever tmt story  is any indication in their 1984 debut  the turtles faced off against the  shredder also known as orokusaki in a  rooftop battle that ended in his  off-screen death some time later the  villain returned to pester the turtles  anew resurrected by the foot clan in a  final showdown leonardo managed to cut  off the shredder's head seemingly  killing him for good but the shredder's  spectre would continue to haunt the  brothers however with raphael even  adopting the villain's mantle at one  point of course in virtually every other  incarnation of the turtles the shredder  has been portrayed as their main  antagonist nowadays many recognize the  shredder as the yin to the turtles yang  like the joker to batman or lex luthor  to superman not too bad for a guy named  after an office machine and covered with  glorified cheese graters  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite turtles are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

